It's holding retrograde.

1132
00:58:11,300 --> 00:58:14,200
As soon as I go back to 1x on speed.

1133
00:58:14,480 --> 00:58:17,460
So I guess this doesn't work when you're at speeds above 1x.

1134
00:58:21,190 --> 00:58:22,270
That makes sense, I guess.

1135
00:58:23,190 --> 00:58:26,930
Uh-oh.

1136
00:58:26,930 --> 00:58:29,250
Oh, I don't like that we're going on the dark side here.

1137
00:58:29,390 --> 00:58:30,810
But I think we're gonna pop out...

1138
00:58:32,990 --> 00:58:34,210
In a good spot here.

1139
00:58:38,220 --> 00:58:39,560
Going a little faster.

1140
00:58:46,630 --> 00:58:47,370
So dark.

1141
00:58:48,590 --> 00:58:51,410
It says 160,000, but...

1142
00:58:51,950 --> 00:58:53,670
I'm still afraid of hitting a mountain or something.

1143
00:58:53,810 --> 00:58:54,590
Because I can't see anything.

1144
00:58:55,570 --> 00:58:57,530
I know that's not gonna happen, but...

1145
00:58:58,270 --> 00:58:59,190
That's what I'm thinking.

1146
00:59:00,350 --> 00:59:02,390
Oh, I should also, uh...

1147
00:59:02,930 --> 00:59:04,210
So periapsis 56.

1148
00:59:06,070 --> 00:59:08,350
Maybe I should burn a little more, just to be safe.

1149
00:59:12,460 --> 00:59:13,700
Use up all the fuel, maybe.

1150
00:59:27,180 --> 00:59:28,100
That's probably fine.

1151
00:59:28,360 --> 00:59:29,980
I mean, we're gonna be slowing down quite a bit.

1152
00:59:32,520 --> 00:59:33,440
I'm gonna detach.

1153
00:59:34,720 --> 00:59:35,320
You ready?

1154
00:59:40,160 --> 00:59:40,600
Damn.

1155
00:59:41,480 --> 00:59:41,920
Okay.

1156
00:59:42,820 --> 00:59:43,980
We're at 70-ish...

1157
00:59:46,000 --> 00:59:46,440
Kilometers.

1158
00:59:51,540 --> 00:59:52,800
Okay, we're at 1x now.

1159
00:59:53,860 --> 00:59:54,600
Oh, man.

1160
00:59:56,340 --> 00:59:57,820
It's already starting to heat.

1161
01:00:01,620 --> 01:00:02,580
This thing is, too.

1162
01:00:05,560 --> 01:00:08,320
This thing will overtake us, because it's gonna become like a missile.

1163
01:00:09,500 --> 01:00:10,900
And it's gonna fly ahead of us.

1164
01:00:11,300 --> 01:00:12,100
When we get down.

1165
01:00:23,780 --> 01:00:25,220
I'm afraid of fast-forwarding.

1166
01:00:36,490 --> 01:00:38,570
Imagine if you do this, and you forget the heat shield.

1167
01:00:40,390 --> 01:00:41,630
You're just like, oh, wait, shit.

1168
01:00:42,050 --> 01:00:42,910
I guess we're dead.

1169
01:00:44,250 --> 01:00:44,850
God damn.

1170
01:00:48,670 --> 01:00:50,530
Please let us pop out on the bright side.

1171
01:00:55,500 --> 01:00:56,960
None of this darkness crap.

1172
01:00:57,200 --> 01:00:57,460
Come on.

1173
01:00:58,560 --> 01:01:00,140
We're not slowing down a lot.

1174
01:01:02,820 --> 01:01:03,300
But...

1175
01:01:04,500 --> 01:01:05,340
Look at this thing.

1176
01:01:07,100 --> 01:01:08,000
I mean, we're...

1177
01:01:08,000 --> 01:01:11,060
If we don't slow it down enough, we're gonna come back around.

1178
01:01:12,460 --> 01:01:13,620
Slower than before, right?

1179
01:01:18,120 --> 01:01:18,780
Oh, my God.

1180
01:01:18,820 --> 01:01:19,940
I can't see nothing.

1181
01:01:23,820 --> 01:01:24,300
Okay.

1182
01:01:31,880 --> 01:01:34,140
Yeah, we're starting to exit the atmosphere again.

1183
01:01:34,860 --> 01:01:36,480
We did not slow down enough.

1184
01:01:37,040 --> 01:01:38,420
I knew I should have burned more.

1185
01:01:38,800 --> 01:01:39,180
Damn it.

1186
01:01:41,660 --> 01:01:43,260
But hey, maybe this is actually a good thing.

1187
01:01:43,640 --> 01:01:46,060
Because this means we're not gonna come in as steep.

1188
01:01:46,260 --> 01:01:48,240
You know, and we bleed off some energy now.

1189
01:01:48,480 --> 01:01:51,220
The next time we come back around, it's not gonna be as crazy.

1190
01:01:52,260 --> 01:01:54,280
This may actually be kinda smart.

1191
01:01:55,160 --> 01:01:56,140
I'm gonna speed up.

1192
01:01:58,620 --> 01:01:59,880
I can't go more than four.

1193
01:02:05,020 --> 01:02:05,780
There's the moon.

1194
01:02:07,560 --> 01:02:08,000
Planets.

1195
01:02:09,560 --> 01:02:11,000
Yeah, now we're back in space.

1196
01:02:11,340 --> 01:02:12,080
Oh, man.

1197
01:02:12,700 --> 01:02:13,740
I'm sorry, Valentina.

1198
01:02:14,680 --> 01:02:16,940
Your dinner's gonna have to wait a little longer.

1199
01:02:18,320 --> 01:02:20,660
She's been underway almost a week.

1200
01:02:20,940 --> 01:02:22,760
Look, it's six days now, mission time.

1201
01:02:26,120 --> 01:02:28,140
Why can't I go faster?

1202
01:02:36,450 --> 01:02:37,650
Oh, now it works.

1203
01:02:39,070 --> 01:02:39,510
Hundreds.

1204
01:02:42,390 --> 01:02:42,950
Weeeee!

1205
01:02:47,070 --> 01:02:47,970
Careful now.

1206
01:02:49,870 --> 01:02:51,910
I think these lines are my connections.

1207
01:03:00,130 --> 01:03:01,670
Okay, we're still very far.

1208
01:03:04,680 --> 01:03:07,180
Well, you could see, like, altitude in this view.

1209
01:03:07,880 --> 01:03:08,500
Can I?

1210
01:03:15,300 --> 01:03:15,740
Somehow?

1211
01:03:16,100 --> 01:03:16,780
Maybe I can't.

1212
01:03:21,190 --> 01:03:22,850
Like, I don't need this right here.

1213
01:03:22,930 --> 01:03:23,930
I need altitude.

1214
01:03:26,650 --> 01:03:27,670
How far down are we?

1215
01:03:29,050 --> 01:03:29,930
Hundred kilometers.

1216
01:03:32,110 --> 01:03:33,090
Just wait a bit.

1217
01:03:34,310 --> 01:03:35,990
So, around 70 is when we enter.

1218
01:03:37,550 --> 01:03:39,530
And the needle will start moving on atmosphere.

1219
01:03:44,040 --> 01:03:44,400
There.

1220
01:03:44,620 --> 01:03:44,700
There.

1221
01:03:44,700 --> 01:03:44,740
See?

1222
01:03:50,630 --> 01:03:52,010
This time we're a little slower.

1223
01:04:00,780 --> 01:04:01,800
I'm gonna speed up, man.

1224
01:04:09,040 --> 01:04:10,660
This is a crazy return trip.

1225
01:04:12,360 --> 01:04:13,560
Okay, I learned my lesson, though.

1226
01:04:13,780 --> 01:04:16,880
When you wanna return home, you gotta go to less than...

1227
01:04:17,740 --> 01:04:18,460
57 kilometers.

1228
01:04:19,320 --> 01:04:20,940
Yeah, see, now we're starting to exit again.

1229
01:04:21,080 --> 01:04:21,700
Are you kidding me?

1230
01:04:23,380 --> 01:04:25,440
Okay, we're gonna have to do this a couple times, I guess.

1231
01:04:28,160 --> 01:04:29,940
But I think we're gonna go home safe.

1232
01:04:32,440 --> 01:04:33,160
Sorry, Valentina.

1233
01:04:33,480 --> 01:04:34,700
Lunch is gonna wait.

1234
01:04:34,880 --> 01:04:35,740
Yeah, we have to skip dinner.

1235
01:04:41,630 --> 01:04:43,110
Oh, I think it's maybe when you're in space.

1236
01:04:43,230 --> 01:04:43,710
Then you can do it.

1237
01:04:44,510 --> 01:04:45,750
For some reason, you have to go back.

1238
01:04:45,850 --> 01:04:46,690
And then go back up.

1239
01:04:46,790 --> 01:04:47,230
It's kinda weird.

1240
01:04:49,590 --> 01:04:49,950
50x.

1241
01:04:51,690 --> 01:04:52,050
Hundred.

1242
01:04:52,410 --> 01:04:52,770
Whee!

1243
01:04:53,730 --> 01:04:54,570
Back we go.

1244
01:04:59,930 --> 01:05:01,490
And I guess now is the atmosphere.

1245
01:05:01,650 --> 01:05:03,070
It's already doing it automatically.

1246
01:05:03,070 --> 01:05:03,990
It's actually kinda nice.

1247
01:05:07,320 --> 01:05:08,340
Here we go again!

1248
01:05:09,000 --> 01:05:11,540
This time we're at 2,600 meters per second.

1249
01:05:19,390 --> 01:05:21,250
Dude, how many times are we gonna have to do this?

1250
01:05:23,690 --> 01:05:24,910
We're at 4x now.

1251
01:05:27,470 --> 01:05:29,210
We're bleeding off so little every time.

1252
01:05:36,400 --> 01:05:37,360
Why did I...

1253
01:05:37,360 --> 01:05:38,160
You know what?

1254
01:05:38,200 --> 01:05:40,380
I shouldn't have disregarded my engines.

1255
01:05:40,620 --> 01:05:42,200
Or, like, disconnected them.

1256
01:05:42,260 --> 01:05:43,340
I still had some fuel left.

1257
01:05:45,240 --> 01:05:46,360
But I guess I couldn't have known.

1258
01:05:49,290 --> 01:05:49,730
Hmm.

1259
01:05:54,450 --> 01:05:55,710
I mean, look at this over here.

1260
01:05:56,110 --> 01:05:56,810
Hey, you know what?

1261
01:05:56,930 --> 01:05:59,030
I actually think we're gonna get home on this side.

1262
01:05:59,410 --> 01:06:04,010
We are actually gonna end up home on the bright side of the planet.

1263
01:06:04,670 --> 01:06:06,430
It sounds ridiculous, but it's true.

1264
01:06:07,450 --> 01:06:09,550
Because we're not gonna slow down over here anytime soon.

1265
01:06:14,380 --> 01:06:17,060
Okay, so when we hit 70, we can start to do this.

1266
01:06:18,740 --> 01:06:19,500
Dude, again?

1267
01:06:19,500 --> 01:06:20,000
Look at that!

1268
01:06:20,620 --> 01:06:23,120
Well, I guess chances of when you go in the same plane...

1269
01:06:23,500 --> 01:06:25,280
...of seeing it happen is kinda high, I guess.

1270
01:06:27,060 --> 01:06:28,100
I can't believe it.

1271
01:06:31,150 --> 01:06:32,090
Another eclipse.

1272
01:06:36,620 --> 01:06:38,580
Valentina has been on a journey, man.

1273
01:06:38,640 --> 01:06:39,600
This has been an adventure.

1274
01:06:43,660 --> 01:06:45,440
You see how the, uh...

1275
01:06:45,440 --> 01:06:47,700
...the lines here shift depending on where you are?

1276
01:06:49,120 --> 01:06:51,720
This is how we maintain connection with, uh...

1277
01:06:51,720 --> 01:06:52,520
...the space center.

1278
01:06:52,940 --> 01:06:54,620
There's different ones around the globe.

1279
01:06:54,880 --> 01:06:55,780
That's actually so cool.

1280
01:07:01,810 --> 01:07:02,790
Let's see if this is enough.

1281
01:07:04,710 --> 01:07:05,430
2,400.

1282
01:07:07,410 --> 01:07:08,010
Think about it.

1283
01:07:08,070 --> 01:07:09,190
The slower we move...

1284
01:07:09,570 --> 01:07:11,470
...uh, the more time we spend in the atmosphere.

1285
01:07:12,990 --> 01:07:15,090
But of course, the faster you move, uh...

1286
01:07:15,090 --> 01:07:16,130
...uh, the more drag matters.

1287
01:07:16,170 --> 01:07:17,930
I think it goes by the velocity square.

1288
01:07:18,070 --> 01:07:20,630
So I don't actually know which one of those two terms matter most.

1289
01:07:21,490 --> 01:07:22,270
In this case.

1290
01:07:23,430 --> 01:07:24,450
Well, we'll find out.

1291
01:07:38,140 --> 01:07:39,460
Oh, we're slowing down a lot now.

1292
01:07:39,880 --> 01:07:42,260
I guess we came a little further down this time, so...

1293
01:07:42,260 --> 01:07:43,300
...the air is more dense.

1294
01:07:46,580 --> 01:07:47,420
Yeah, look at that!

1295
01:07:47,720 --> 01:07:47,960
Look!

1296
01:07:48,060 --> 01:07:48,360
You see that?

1297
01:07:48,540 --> 01:07:49,960
Oh, we're totally coming down now.

1298
01:07:50,960 --> 01:07:51,640
This is it!

1299
01:07:52,520 --> 01:07:53,900
Hold on to your hats and goggles!

1300
01:07:55,720 --> 01:07:57,220
I'm gonna go 1x on this.

1301
01:08:05,310 --> 01:08:06,590
We're finally coming home!

1302
01:08:11,720 --> 01:08:12,380
There we go.

1303
01:08:14,140 --> 01:08:16,100
Don't even need to look at the UI.

1304
01:08:16,780 --> 01:08:18,460
Now Jesus takes the wheel, you know?

1305
01:08:24,170 --> 01:08:25,970
Also, what happened to my...

1306
01:08:25,970 --> 01:08:26,510
...stage?

1307
01:08:29,980 --> 01:08:31,140
It's not that back there.

1308
01:08:31,220 --> 01:08:31,620
That's me.

1309
01:08:32,980 --> 01:08:34,180
I wonder where it is.

1310
01:08:35,720 --> 01:08:37,140
It's probably off somewhere else.

1311
01:08:41,350 --> 01:08:41,950
Oh, yeah.

1312
01:08:44,920 --> 01:08:46,840
Wait, let me actually look at the heat shield.

1313
01:08:48,060 --> 01:08:49,020
Oh, look at this!

1314
01:08:51,680 --> 01:08:52,880
It's actually kind of low.

1315
01:08:56,010 --> 01:08:57,590
Ah, we'll make it, right?

1316
01:08:59,230 --> 01:09:02,630
We've gone past this planet so many times now, there's surely enough for this one.

1317
01:09:06,160 --> 01:09:07,000
Should be okay.

1318
01:09:12,700 --> 01:09:19,520
So I wonder if this actually means that as long as you have a blader left, you can survive any heat.

1319
01:09:20,760 --> 01:09:24,580
Or maybe there's like a maximum heat for this heat shield and you can get a better heat shield.

1320
01:09:25,460 --> 01:09:26,020
You know?

1321
01:09:28,970 --> 01:09:30,010
I guess it means...

1322
01:09:30,010 --> 01:09:30,910
I think it's the first.

1323
01:09:32,130 --> 01:09:33,490
That would make the most sense.

1324
01:09:37,020 --> 01:09:39,000
I don't want to land on the dark side, man!

1325
01:09:39,220 --> 01:09:39,420
Fuck!

1326
01:09:39,600 --> 01:09:40,260
After this trip?

1327
01:09:41,420 --> 01:09:42,280
That's so sad.

1328
01:09:51,150 --> 01:09:53,390
Actually, this was so textbook in a way.

1329
01:09:53,590 --> 01:09:54,730
The way we came home here.

1330
01:09:55,130 --> 01:09:59,050
I mean, except the, you know, skipping across the atmosphere a couple times.

1331
01:10:01,150 --> 01:10:03,930
Ignoring that, I think it went pretty dang well.

1332
01:10:05,550 --> 01:10:06,350
Where are we?

1333
01:10:09,350 --> 01:10:10,470
In the middle of nowhere.

1334
01:10:13,550 --> 01:10:18,690
Valentina, you're probably going to have to wait a couple more weeks in this capsule in the middle of nowhere for the rescue team.

1335
01:10:19,490 --> 01:10:20,170
I'm sorry.

1336
01:10:22,830 --> 01:10:23,270
Shoots!

1337
01:10:25,150 --> 01:10:26,310
The drogues are up.

1338
01:10:30,170 --> 01:10:32,130
I think we can safely deploy...

1339
01:10:33,290 --> 01:10:34,570
The main chute as well.

1340
01:10:37,070 --> 01:10:38,870
I think we're going to hit the...

1341
01:10:38,870 --> 01:10:39,070
Hey!

1342
01:10:39,530 --> 01:10:40,330
We're not going to splash down.

1343
01:10:40,410 --> 01:10:42,310
We're going to hit the ground here.

1344
01:10:42,650 --> 01:10:42,870
Nice.

1345
01:10:47,330 --> 01:10:49,850
At least her snacks are going to stay dry.

1346
01:10:54,060 --> 01:10:54,860
There they go.

1347
01:10:58,590 --> 01:10:59,570
This ambient light.

1348
01:10:59,610 --> 01:11:00,250
Where is this coming from?

1349
01:11:00,330 --> 01:11:01,750
Why is the ground so visible?

1350
01:11:02,110 --> 01:11:03,450
What is that white stuff?

1351
01:11:05,090 --> 01:11:06,470
Is there any right below me?

1352
01:11:08,510 --> 01:11:10,390
We have to investigate this at some point.

1353
01:11:12,230 --> 01:11:13,570
Because this is a mystery.

1354
01:11:14,290 --> 01:11:15,690
Like, what are these things?

1355
01:11:17,050 --> 01:11:18,010
Scattered all over.

1356
01:11:27,070 --> 01:11:28,610
I can't see anything out the window.

1357
01:11:35,550 --> 01:11:37,230
It still hasn't said anything.

1358
01:11:37,230 --> 01:11:38,090
Maybe when we land.

1359
01:11:39,310 --> 01:11:40,170
Let's pay attention.

1360
01:11:44,940 --> 01:11:46,200
Wait, it says 200 meters.

1361
01:11:46,320 --> 01:11:46,720
Is this...

1362
01:11:46,720 --> 01:11:47,900
Oh, it's got to be, like, sea level.

1363
01:11:50,940 --> 01:11:51,440
Return...

1364
01:11:53,200 --> 01:11:54,200
Uh-oh.

1365
01:11:55,580 --> 01:11:56,580
Uh-oh.

1366
01:11:59,860 --> 01:12:00,620
Let's see.

1367
01:12:06,340 --> 01:12:08,160
22.8 signs earned.

1368
01:12:08,340 --> 01:12:08,680
Nice.

1369
01:12:09,900 --> 01:12:11,540
We got all of this back.

1370
01:12:12,640 --> 01:12:14,300
Two experience gains!

1371
01:12:14,300 --> 01:12:15,240
I mean...

1372
01:12:15,240 --> 01:12:16,480
I better...

1373
01:12:16,480 --> 01:12:17,760
Okay, we need to see this now.

1374
01:12:17,940 --> 01:12:19,340
First, warp to sunrise.

1375
01:12:19,640 --> 01:12:21,140
So we can actually get some light.

1376
01:12:24,860 --> 01:12:25,160
Oh.

1377
01:12:25,500 --> 01:12:26,120
Brief shower.

1378
01:12:27,020 --> 01:12:28,260
There we go.

1379
01:12:28,440 --> 01:12:29,300
Oh, that's so much better.

1380
01:12:29,900 --> 01:12:30,300
Okay.

1381
01:12:30,880 --> 01:12:31,580
Mission control.

1382
01:12:33,560 --> 01:12:33,960
Hey!

1383
01:12:34,260 --> 01:12:34,640
Oh, wait.

1384
01:12:34,800 --> 01:12:36,120
Did we actually do it, then?

1385
01:12:36,580 --> 01:12:38,260
Or did we just do it partially?

1386
01:12:42,380 --> 01:12:42,780
Yeah!

1387
01:12:43,340 --> 01:12:44,660
Okay, so it does mean...

1388
01:12:44,660 --> 01:12:45,480
You've got to bring it back.

1389
01:12:46,560 --> 01:12:46,960
Nice.

1390
01:12:48,780 --> 01:12:49,180
Okay.

1391
01:12:50,340 --> 01:12:50,880
So, wait.

1392
01:12:50,900 --> 01:12:51,700
How much money do we have?

1393
01:12:51,700 --> 01:12:54,480
Oh, 300,000!

1394
01:12:54,680 --> 01:12:55,560
We are saved!

1395
01:12:56,240 --> 01:12:58,700
The space program is active!

1396
01:12:59,420 --> 01:13:01,260
We are so active!

1397
01:13:02,120 --> 01:13:03,340
Let's see here.

1398
01:13:04,800 --> 01:13:05,380
What...

1399
01:13:05,380 --> 01:13:07,480
Rescue Carson from orbit of Kerman!

1400
01:13:09,400 --> 01:13:10,340
I mean, Kerman.

1401
01:13:12,020 --> 01:13:19,200
As a consequence of the somewhat worse than average accident at Research and Development Department, we've been forced to look for some outside help.

1402
01:13:19,480 --> 01:13:24,740
We've been performing a lot of experiments with leaving Kerbals in space for extended periods of time.

1403
